  "id": "2hFJUcyUeSqVZs23",
  "name": "EP: Monthly Patch Scheduler -> reset_pending",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6e20cdb7-6f8f-4a66-bf40-164b33c5dc34",
      "name": "Format Failure Message",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const t = $('Reset patch_status=pending via IaC API').item.json;\nconst text = `🔴 Monthly patch scheduler FAILED to reset patch_status in NetBox. No VMs will be patched this cycle.\\nCheck IaC API logs — task ${t.task_id}.`;\nreturn [{ json: { txn_id: 'patchcycle-fail-' + Date.now(), matrixPayload: { msgtype: 'm.text', body: text } } }];",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "position": [
        1750,
        400
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "83053375-ce8c-43f1-823b-9e36e8f9d4b9",
      "name": "Format Success Message",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const text = '🗓️ Monthly patch cycle started — patch_status=pending set on all registered patchable VMs. Watch this room over the next hour for individual VM results (each patches one at a time, snapshot-backed, auto-rolled-back on failure).';\nreturn [{ json: { txn_id: 'patchcycle-ok-' + Date.now(), matrixPayload: { msgtype: 'm.text', body: text } } }];",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "position": [
        1750,
        200
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "63a929eb-1482-4211-99b7-7ad604954524",
      "name": "Monthly (15th, 03:00)",
      "notes": "CHANGED 2026-08-17: was weekly (every Monday) -> monthly, per explicit request:\npatch roughly once a month, about 1-2 weeks after updates typically land, giving\nthem time to shake out upstream before this fleet applies them unattended.\nDebian/Ubuntu don't have a single 'Patch Tuesday' the way Windows does, so this\npicks a fixed, easy-to-reason-about day (the 15th) as a ~2-week-into-the-month\nbuffer rather than trying to track individual CVE/release calendars. Adjust the\nday here if a different reference point is wanted.\n\nThis is the piece that was missing: nothing previously set patch_status=pending\non a schedule. rolling_update.yml + patch_trigger.json already existed and\nworked, but only fired when something manually flipped a VM to pending in\nNetBox. This workflow closes the loop: monthly, it resets patch_status=pending\non all patchable VMs via netbox_setup_patch_fields.yml --tags reset_pending.\nNetBox's existing Event Rule then fires the 'NetBox Patch Trigger' webhook per\nVM exactly as if a human had done it — full snapshot/health-check/rollback\nsafety, no new code path.\n\nZERO-DAY / OUT-OF-BAND PATCHING: this monthly cycle is NOT the mechanism for\nan urgent CVE — see the separate 'EP: Zero-Day Patch Warning' workflow, which\nposts an immediate Matrix warning and can be used to hand-trigger rolling_update.yml\nfor just the affected host(s) without waiting for this schedule.",
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "expression": "0 3 15 * *",
              "field": "cronExpression"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "position": [
        250,
        300
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "cqzqjeK3jtlIBvYD",
          "name": "Matrix Bot Bearer"
        }
      },
